<title>UK: McCarthy &amp; Stone rallies on interim results.</title>
<headline>McCarthy &amp; Stone rallies on interim results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in property development firm McCarthy &amp; Stone Plc advanced briskly on Tuesday after it published interim results, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1010 GMT McCarthy &amp; Stone shares were up 7.5 pence at 126p bid, a fresh high for the stock, on volume of 400,000.</p>
<p>&quot;The results look strong and we could see some (profit) upgrades,&quot; a dealer at a British bank said.</p>
<p>McCarthy &amp; Stone earlier posted first-half profits of 6.0 million stg, against 2.1 million stg last time and said its gross margin increased to 37 percent from 33 percent.</p>
<p>--Dan Lalor, London newsroom +44 171 542-7717</p>
</text>
